  "sections": [
    {
      "key": "distribution",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/oryzias_celebensis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Oryzias celebensis, the Celebes rice fish, originates from Indonesia, where it inhabits the island of Celebes.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "habitat",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/oryzias_celebensis_en/",
      "html": "<p>It lives in standing to slowly flowing waters which are heavily planted.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "aquariumSize",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/oryzias_celebensis_en/",
      "html": "<p>It grows to approximately 5 cm and needs a free swimming area and retreat possibilities.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "waterConditions",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/oryzias_celebensis_en/",
      "html": "<p>Oryzias celebensis prefers rather high pH values. Optimal water should exhibit a pH of 8 and also a not too small water hardness (10 dGH).</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "behaviour",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/oryzias_celebensis_en/",
      "html": "<p>This is a schooling fish that needs a free swimming area and retreat possibilities, since rice fish occasionally tend to become somewhat quarrelsome among themselves.</p>"
    },
    {
      "key": "reproduction",
      "source": "glaser",
      "sourceUrl": "https://www.aquariumglaser.de/en/18-toothcarps-killis-and-livebearers/oryzias_celebensis_en/",
      "html": "<p>In such water, breeding of rice fish is possible. Interestingly, the female carries the eggs for several hours before attaching them to a substrate. Raising the fry should not be difficult.</p>"
    }
  ],
